          "source_text_sha256": "429a72fbc411e36e43e35ec2175e875614f0d2ad50041de663efda891edcf2db",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On July 8, 2014, at 9:33 PM, a witness is intrigued by the straight-line passage of a very bright rectangular shape. During the 6 to 8 seconds of observation, the fast object moves silently. No other witnesses were reported. The witness observes a yellow rectangle advancing above the horizon. The sun has set for 8 minutes. The witness looks towards the southeast and sees the object pass from left to right (refer to his drawings). A plane, illuminated from the side by the setting sun, appears as a very bright rectangle (the wings do not receive the sun's rays directly, the drift, level, reflects the sun in a different direction than the cylindrical fuselage). The gray halo around the object may be an atmospheric optical phenomenon, quite complex at low elevation, or a local blinding phenomenon at the observer's eye level. The Flightradar record indicates an airplane that could be the subject of this observation: the AF Orly-Marseille flight in approach to Marignane. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": observation of an airplane at sunset.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "37695923d08dfaa2b5cee5e5d0565a282ee10a0677934b1d61f8135ba6d7f3cb"
        }
